$DIR/main.p:16:11: cannot keep the closure mk(42 + i) returns past this iteration of the loop: it is stored in first, declared outside the loop (main.p:14)
    A function that returns a closure builds it in a region its caller provides
    (spec section 11.5). The region of a call in a loop is part of this frame,
    and the call uses the same region on every iteration, so the closure mk(42 +
    i) returns on one iteration is overwritten on the next. Keeping it past the
    iteration, in first, declared outside the loop (main.p:14), would leave it
    changing under you.
    Use the closure within the iteration, or declare the variable that holds it
    inside the loop.
    Go allocates each closure on the heap. Plutonium builds it in the caller's
    frame, which has room for one closure per call site.
    (see "Closures and their regions" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3101" for a longer explanation)
